{"id": 12019, "stem": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-text\"><span><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-100\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">A</mark> 14-year-old boy with chronic anemia is being evaluated after experiencing several episodes of chest, back, and extremity pain.\u00a0 Peripheral blood smear reveals sickle-shaped red blood cells.\u00a0 Genetic testing shows that the patient is homozygous for a point mutation in the beta-globin gene, resulting in a glutamic acid to valine substitution at position 6.\u00a0 Sequencing the affected DNA would most likely reveal which of the following changes?\u00a0 (The genetic code is shown in the figure below.)</p><div id=\"div_t130049\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"relative max-w-full\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-r from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute right-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-l from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div class=\"max-w-full overflow-x-auto [&amp;_td]:min-w-[8rem] [&amp;_th]:min-w-[8rem]\"><table class=\"border bg-transparent dark:text-white border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white hover:bg-transparent warm:hover:bg-transparent dark:hover:bg-transparent cursor-default mt-2 mb-3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tbody styl